    question: "What is index signature?",
    idealAnswer: "**Index signatures** in TypeScript allow you to define types for objects that can have arbitrary string or number keys with consistent value types. They're useful for dictionary-like objects and dynamic property access.\n\n**Basic Syntax:**\n```typescript\ninterface InterfaceName {\n  [key: KeyType]: ValueType;\n}\n```\n\n**String Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface StringDictionary {\n  [key: string]: string;\n}\n\nconst dictionary: StringDictionary = {\n  name: \"John\",\n  email: \"john@example.com\",\n  phone: \"123-456-7890\"\n};\n\n// Dynamic access\nfunction getValue(obj: StringDictionary, key: string): string {\n  return obj[key];\n}\n\nconsole.log(getValue(dictionary, \"name\")); // \"John\"\n```\n\n**Number Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface NumberArray {\n  [index: number]: string;\n}\n\nconst arrayLike: NumberArray = {\n  0: \"first\",\n  1: \"second\",\n  2: \"third\"\n};\n\nconsole.log(arrayLike[0]); // \"first\"\nconsole.log(arrayLike[1]); // \"second\"\n```\n\n**Mixed Properties with Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface User {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  [key: string]: any; // Allow any other string properties\n}\n\nconst user: User = {\n  id: 1,\n  name: \"John\",\n  email: \"john@example.com\", // Additional property\n  age: 30,                  // Additional property\n  isAdmin: true              // Additional property\n};\n```\n\n**Union Types in Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface FlexibleDictionary {\n  [key: string]: string | number | boolean;\n}\n\nconst flexDict: FlexibleDictionary = {\n  name: \"John\",\n  age: 30,\n  isActive: true,\n  score: 95.5\n};\n```\n\n**Readonly Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface ReadonlyStringDict {\n  readonly [key: string]: string;\n}\n\nconst constants: ReadonlyStringDict = {\n  PI: \"3.14159\",\n  E: \"2.71828\",\n  GOLDEN_RATIO: \"1.61803\"\n};\n\n// constants.PI = \"3.14\"; // Error - readonly\n```\n\n**Generic Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface Dictionary<T> {\n  [key: string]: T;\n}\n\nconst stringDict: Dictionary<string> = {\n  hello: \"world\",\n  foo: \"bar\"\n};\n\nconst numberDict: Dictionary<number> = {\n  count: 42,\n  total: 100\n};\n\nconst boolDict: Dictionary<boolean> = {\n  isActive: true,\n  isVisible: false\n};\n```\n\n**Constrained Index Signatures:**\n```typescript\ninterface StringKeyDictionary<T extends string | number> {\n  [key: string]: T;\n}\n\nconst mixedDict: StringKeyDictionary<string | number> = {\n  name: \"John\",\n  age: 30,\n  score: 95.5\n};\n```\n\n**Practical Examples:**\n\n**1. HTTP Headers:**\n```typescript\ninterface HttpHeaders {\n  [header: string]: string;\n}\n\nfunction createHeaders(headers: HttpHeaders): HttpHeaders {\n  return {\n    'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n    'Accept': 'application/json',\n    ...headers\n  };\n}\n\nconst customHeaders = createHeaders({\n  'Authorization': 'Bearer token123',\n  'X-Custom-Header': 'custom-value'\n});\n```\n\n**2. Configuration Objects:**\n```typescript\ninterface Config {\n  apiUrl: string;\n  timeout: number;\n  [key: string]: string | number | boolean;\n}\n\nconst appConfig: Config = {\n  apiUrl: 'https://api.example.com',\n  timeout: 5000,\n  debug: true,\n  maxRetries: 3,\n  enableLogging: false\n};\n```\n\n**3. Form Data:**\n```typescript\ninterface FormData {\n  [fieldName: string]: string | string[] | number | boolean;\n}\n\nfunction processFormData(data: FormData): void {\n  Object.entries(data).forEach(([key, value]) => {\n    console.log(`${key}: ${value}`);\n  });\n}\n\nconst formSubmission: FormData = {\n  username: 'john_doe',\n  email: 'john@example.com',\n  age: 30,\n  interests: ['coding', 'music'],\n  newsletter: true\n};\n```\n\n**4. Cache Implementation:**\n```typescript\nclass SimpleCache<T> {\n  private cache: { [key: string]: T } = {};\n  \n  set(key: string, value: T): void {\n    this.cache[key] = value;\n  }\n  \n  get(key: string): T | undefined {\n    return this.cache[key];\n  }\n  \n  has(key: string): boolean {\n    return key in this.cache;\n  }\n  \n  clear(): void {\n    this.cache = {};\n  }\n}\n\nconst userCache = new SimpleCache<User>();\nuserCache.set('user_1', { id: 1, name: 'John' });\n```\n\n**5. API Response Wrapper:**\n```typescript\ninterface ApiResponse<T> {\n  data: T;\n  status: number;\n  message: string;\n  metadata: { [key: string]: any };\n}\n\nfunction handleResponse<T>(response: ApiResponse<T>): void {\n  console.log('Status:', response.status);\n  console.log('Message:', response.message);\n  console.log('Data:', response.data);\n  \n  // Dynamic metadata\n  if (response.metadata.totalCount) {\n    console.log('Total items:', response.metadata.totalCount);\n  }\n  \n  if (response.metadata.nextPage) {\n    console.log('Next page:', response.metadata.nextPage);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Index Signatures vs Record Type:**\n```typescript\n// Index signature\ninterface StringIndex {\n  [key: string]: number;\n}\n\n// Record utility type (often preferred)\ntype StringRecord = Record<string, number>;\n\n// Both are equivalent\nconst obj1: StringIndex = { a: 1, b: 2 };\nconst obj2: StringRecord = { a: 1, b: 2 };\n```\n\n**Limitations and Rules:**\n```typescript\n// Index signature type must match all property types\ninterface Mixed {\n  name: string;\n  [key: string]: number; // Error: Property 'name' of type 'string' is not assignable to string index type 'number'\n}\n\n// Correct way - use union type\ninterface CorrectMixed {\n  name: string;\n  [key: string]: string | number;\n}\n\n// Or use 'any' for flexibility\ninterface FlexibleMixed {\n  name: string;\n  [key: string]: any;\n}\n```\n\n**Benefits of Index Signatures:**\n- **Flexibility**: Handle dynamic property names\n- **Dictionary Pattern**: Create dictionary-like objects\n- **API Compatibility**: Work with JSON objects of varying structures\n- **Dynamic Data**: Handle data from databases or external APIs\n- **Type Safety**: Still provide type checking for values\n\n**When to Use Index Signatures:**\n- Dictionary-like data structures\n- HTTP headers and query parameters\n- Configuration objects with dynamic keys\n- Form data processing\n- Cache implementations\n- When working with JSON from external sources"
